    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0571" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.361/6–2651: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Deputy Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gross</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-06-26T19:18:00-04:00">June 26, 1951—7:18
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1722. Re efforts to see Malik. Round-up of activities today re Deptel 1019, June
                    25, reported separately by memo to Hickerson.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d365-f1"/> I
                    would appreciate guidance from Dept whether to make a renewed effort to <pb
                        facs="0572" n="556" xml:id="pg556"/> see Malik during morning of June 27. I
                    am continuing to concert closely with Jebb, who is making no separate effort to
                    establish contact with Malik.</p>
                <p>In the event that our efforts to see Malik do not succeed, I would like
                    instructions re attitude to take at SC dinner Thurs night.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d365-f2"/> There is no indication, at least as yet, that Malik will
                    be unable to attend the dinner.</p>
                <p>Lie, who is returning to New York morning June 27, will undoubtedly wish to see
                    me urgently. Would appreciate discretion in dealing with him, subject of course
                    to balancing amenity with security.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gross</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d365-f1" n="1" xml:id="d365-f1-content">
                <p>The memorandum is not printed, but the substance of it was communicated to Moscow
                    by the Department in telegram 837, sent at 9 p. m. on June 26 as follows:</p>
                <p>“FYI Gross this morning requested thru Malik’s office an appointment and was
                    informed that Malik was out of town; that they would try to communicate with
                    him, but were not certain they could do so. He has had no further info.”
                    (310.361/6–2651)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d365-f2" n="2" xml:id="d365-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram Unmis 47 from New York, June 29, <ref target="#pg590">p.
                    590</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
